        <html><![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<j:jelly trim="false" xmlns:j="jelly:core" xmlns:g="glide" xmlns:j2="null" xmlns:g2="null">
    <!-- Get values from dialog preferences passed in -->


<!-- Set up form fields and labels -->

<html>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/4.7.0/css/font-awesome.min.css"></link>
<body style="margin-top: 5px; font-size: 14px; margin-left: 20px; line-height: 1.6;">

    <!-- Header -->
    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; border-bottom: 1px solid #e4e8ee; padding-bottom: 16px; margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Check Point" width="220" style="display: block;"></img>
        <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 13px; color: #8a94a6;">Setup &amp; Configuration Guide</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Intro Section -->
    <h2 style="margin: 0 0 16px 0; font-size: 22px; font-weight: 600; color: #1a2332; letter-spacing: -0.3px;">Setting up the Check Point Exposure Management Alerts</h2>

    <p style="margin: 0 0 10px 0; color: #4a5568;">The ServiceNow system administrator is required to provide the API access token in the application.</p>
    <p style="margin: 0 0 10px 0; color: #4a5568;">This enables the application to connect with your Check Point Exposure Management instance.</p>
    <p style="margin: 0 0 10px 0; color: #4a5568;">After the connection is established, the application will import all the available Threat Command alerts to ServiceNow as incidents.</p>
    <p style="margin: 0 0 24px 0; color: #4a5568;">If you do not have an API access token, contact your Check Point Exposure Management administrator.</p>

    <!-- Properties -->
    <h4 style="margin: 0 0 10px 0; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #1a2332;">Properties</h4>
    <ul style="margin: 0 0 24px 0; padding-left: 20px; color: #4a5568;">
        <li style="margin-bottom: 6px;">You must be the ServiceNow system administrator</li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 6px;">You must have a Check Point Exposure Management API access token</li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0;">In the API Token field, enter the API access token</li>
    </ul>

    <!-- Procedure -->
    <h4 style="margin: 0 0 10px 0; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #1a2332;">Procedure</h4>
    <ol style="margin: 0 0 28px 0; padding-left: 20px; color: #4a5568;">
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; padding-left: 4px;">Log in to ServiceNow as a system administrator</li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; padding-left: 4px;">Navigate to&#160;<strong>Configurations</strong></li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; padding-left: 4px;">In the&#160;<strong>API Token</strong>&#160;field, enter the API access token</li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; padding-left: 4px;">In the&#160;<strong>API Environment</strong>&#160;field, enter the API environment</li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; padding-left: 4px;">Click&#160;<strong>Check Connection</strong>. The system validates the API environment and API token</li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; padding-left: 4px;">In the&#160;<strong>Select Type to fetch the Alerts</strong>&#160;field, select the Threat Command alert types to import. (Note: By default, the Type set to All)</li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; padding-left: 4px;">In the&#160;<strong>Select Severity to fetch the Alerts</strong>&#160;field, select the Threat Command alert severities to import. (Note: By default, the Severity set to All)</li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; padding-left: 4px;">From the&#160;<strong>Last Fetch Time</strong>, select the start date to import alerts. (Note: By default, the Last Fetch Time is set to the last 1 month)</li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0; padding-left: 4px;">Click&#160;<strong>Submit</strong>. The system again validates the API environment and API token. Upon successful validation, a job runs that imports all the open alerts from your Check Point Exposure Management instance</li>
    </ol>

    <!-- Contact Section -->
    <div style="border-top: 1px solid #e4e8ee; padding-top: 20px;">
        <h3 style="margin: 0 0 14px 0; font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600; color: #1a2332;">Contact Check Point</h3>
        <p style="margin: 0 0 10px 0; display: flex; align-items: center;">
            <span style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 32px; height: 32px; background: #eff6ff; border-radius: 6px; margin-right: 10px;">
                <i class="fa fa-envelope" style="font-size: 15px; color: #3b82f6;"></i>
            </span>
            <span>Support email:&#160;<a href="mailto:support@cyberint.com" style="color: #3b82f6; text-decoration: none;">support@cyberint.com</a></span>
        </p>
        <p style="margin: 0; display: flex; align-items: center;">
            <span style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 32px; height: 32px; background: #eff6ff; border-radius: 6px; margin-right: 10px;">
                <i class="fa fa-external-link" style="font-size: 15px; color: #3b82f6;"></i>
            </span>
            <a href="https://cyberint.com/customer-support/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" style="color: #3b82f6; text-decoration: none;">For more information, visit the Check Point support page</a>
        </p>
    </div>

</body>
</html>
</j:jelly>]]></html>
